        ],
        "ID": "Stone1",
        "Description": "Model based on the channel flow theory, which states that in any flow channel there is at most only one mobile fluid. Requires two sets of two-phase data: water-oil displacement and gas-oil displacement based on (Stone, H. L.: \"Probability Model for Estimating Three-Phase Relative Permeability\", paper SPE 2116, Journal of Petroleum Technology (1970)) .",
        "Code": "Stone1",
        "AttributionAuthority": "OSDU",
        "AttributionRevision": "evergreen",
